    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive engine for May 10th is headlined by **Bryson Stott** (72.63) and **Taylor Ward** (69.73), both of whom benefit from exceptional matchup conditions. **Bryson Stott** enters today with a massive 18% boost due to Sugano\u2019s shaky 4.73 xERA, and he\u2019s positioned to capitalize on a favorable platoon split. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** is our premier play in a high-ceiling environment; a 16% park factor uplift combined with the weak arm of Severino makes him an elite start despite the marginal platoon drag. **Brendan Donovan** also merits attention at 67.45; leading off against Martin, his 14% platoon edge is the primary driver for a significant performance ceiling today.\n\nIn terms of bench management, **Gavin Sheets** (51.44) was the hardest exclusion from today\u2019s active roster. While his platoon advantage against Leahy is decent, the overall efficiency of our starting utility slots forced his removal to preserve our long-term game caps. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Jung Hoo Lee** (56.23) against Chandler; despite his lead-off status providing a +10% order boost, the presence of an elite catcher with a sub-1.90s pop time forces us to temper expectations regarding his stolen base potential. The rest of the lineup, including **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (63.34) and **Masyn Winn** (62.13), remains stable, though we are keeping a close eye on **Masyn Winn** as he faces the always-tough Buehler; his ability to exploit a slow delivery is his clearest path to a multi-category impact. \n\nThere are no major weather alerts for the slate, but we are cautious regarding **Lawrence Butler** (56.91), who faces the toughest matchup of the day against Akin. His negative 13% platoon adjustment is a significant risk factor, and while his park factor is high, he remains a candidate to be swapped if internal defensive metrics fluctuate before first pitch. We are currently sitting on depth from the likes of **Tyler Freeman**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Drew Gilbert**, but none provide the necessary efficiency floor to displace our starters in today's 5x5 rotation.",
